{"id": "2026-11-23-sports-lugano-stretch-super-league-lead-to-six", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Lugano stretch Super League lead to six", "summary": "Leaders Lugano beat Grasshoppers 2:1 on Saturday 21 November through two late substitutes' goals, answering a 0:5 loss at St", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/fussball/super-league/14-runde-in-der-super-league-reaktion-auf-0-5-klatsche-lugano-schlaegt-gc-knapp-dank-jokern", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Leaders Lugano beat Grasshoppers 2:1 on Saturday 21 November through two late substitutes' goals, answering a 0:5 loss at St. Gallen before the international break, and YB kept pace only by edging Thun 3:2 in the Bernese derby — so the gap stays at six points, 37 to 31 by my tally from the league table (Wikipedia cross-check, not cited). Lugano have won seven of eight home games. Further back, Sion beat Servette for the first time in five years. The sharper story is Basel: on Sunday 22 November they lost 0:2 at home to Luzern, their sixth league game without a goal in nine, and have not won at home since 9 August; coach Slavisa Jokanovic is still waiting for a first win in five league games, and Luzern climbed past Basel into seventh. Captain Xherdan Shaqiri was substituted at half-time, which the coach said was not injury-related.", "why": "A title race that looked open is becoming Lugano's to lose, while one of Switzerland's biggest clubs is drifting in mid-table.", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-sports-lugano-stretch-super-league-lead-to-six", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-21", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FC Lugano", "Young Boys", "FC Basel"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-sports-verstappen-wins-chaotic-las-vegas-gp", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Verstappen wins chaotic Las Vegas GP", "summary": "Max Verstappen converted an inherited pole position into victory after a race of constant lead changes in which Mercedes drivers repeatedly passed and were re-passed; Lando Norris recovered from 11th ", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-las-vegas-gp-report/10876677/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Max Verstappen converted an inherited pole position into victory after a race of constant lead changes in which Mercedes drivers repeatedly passed and were re-passed; Lando Norris recovered from 11th to finish second and Oscar Piastri from 15th on the grid to third. Mercedes' Kimi Antonelli, who qualified fastest but took a five-place engine penalty, finished fourth and George Russell, while attacking for second, locked up and hit the wall on lap 48, falling to ninth. With two races left, Antonelli leads the standings on 402 points to Verstappen's 304, with Hamilton third on 267 and Norris and Russell level on 264 (Autosport standings table). The title itself is already decided: Antonelli, aged 20, clinched it at the Mexico City race, becoming the youngest champion in F1 history per Autosport .", "why": "The fight that remains is for second place: Verstappen is 37 points ahead of Hamilton with Qatar and Abu Dhabi to go.", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-sports-verstappen-wins-chaotic-las-vegas-gp", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-21", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Max Verstappen", "Kimi Antonelli", "Red Bull", "Mercedes"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-sports-ferrari-teammates-collide-again", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Ferrari teammates collide again", "summary": "Charles Leclerc and Lewis Hamilton made contact while fighting each other for sixth place, spinning Hamilton, and each was handed a 10-second penalty during the race", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/vasseur-furious-with-unprofessional-ferrari-clash-and-demands-fresh-talks-after-las-vegas-gp/10876847/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Charles Leclerc and Lewis Hamilton made contact while fighting each other for sixth place, spinning Hamilton, and each was handed a 10-second penalty during the race. Team principal Fred Vasseur called it \"unprofessional\" and said he wants fresh talks with his drivers, two races after the pair also clashed in Mexico. Hamilton finished seventh and Leclerc tenth.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-sports-ferrari-teammates-collide-again", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-21", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ferrari", "Lewis Hamilton", "Charles Leclerc"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-sports-marquez-clinches-eighth-motogp-title", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Marquez clinches eighth MotoGP title", "summary": "Marc Marquez (Ducati) needed only a top-nine finish and rode a deliberately safe race to eighth to secure the 2026 title, drawing level with Giacomo Agostini as the most successful rider in the premie", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/motogp/news/motogp-portuguese-gp-marquez-crowned-2026-champion-as-bezzecchi-wins-tense-race/10876968/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Marc Marquez (Ducati) needed only a top-nine finish and rode a deliberately safe race to eighth to secure the 2026 title, drawing level with Giacomo Agostini as the most successful rider in the premier class by Autosport's count. Marco Bezzecchi won for Aprilia, which took all three podium places. The title had looked inevitable since Jorge Martin's crash at Phillip Island last month.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-sports-marquez-clinches-eighth-motogp-title", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Marc Marquez", "MotoGP", "Aprilia"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-sports-alcaraz-beats-zverev-for-atp-finals", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Alcaraz beats Zverev for ATP Finals", "summary": "Carlos Alcaraz beat Alexander Zverev 6:2, 7:6 (9:7) in the final of the season-ending tournament for the year's eight best players, his first ATP Finals title", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/tennis/atp-tour/atp-finals-final-alcaraz-bezwingt-zverev-und-gewinnt-zum-1-mal-die-atp-finals", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Carlos Alcaraz beat Alexander Zverev 6:2, 7:6 (9:7) in the final of the season-ending tournament for the year's eight best players, his first ATP Finals title. At 23 he becomes the youngest man to have won all four Grand Slams plus the Finals; only Agassi, Federer and Djokovic had done both. It is his 14th straight match win, and he returned from a wrist injury only at the US Open in late August, then took titles at four of the five events since. Zverev, who won his first two Grand Slams this year and finishes as world No. 1, still trails Alcaraz and Jannik Sinner badly in head-to-head results, SRF notes. Alcaraz himself called Zverev the deserving No. 1 for 2026 (BBC Sport interview).", "why": "The ranking says Zverev, but the form of the last three months says Alcaraz — expect that argument to frame the 2027 season.", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-sports-alcaraz-beats-zverev-for-atp-finals", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Carlos Alcaraz", "Alexander Zverev", "ATP Finals"]}
{"id": "2026-11-23-sports-nef-takes-first-world-cup-podium", "date": "2026-11-23", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Nef takes first World Cup podium", "summary": "In his 86th World Cup race, Geneva's Tanguy Nef finished third in the Gurgl slalom, his first podium after years as a regular top-ten finisher", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/ski-alpin/weltcup-maenner/nach-podestpremiere-in-gurgl-emotionaler-nef-mit-ansage-ich-werde-auch-ein-rennen-gewinnen", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "In his 86th World Cup race, Geneva's Tanguy Nef finished third in the Gurgl slalom, his first podium after years as a regular top-ten finisher. Snow and difficult conditions knocked out big names including Lucas Pinheiro Braathen, Henrik Kristoffersen and Atle Lie McGrath before the second run ended. Nef, who debuted in 2018, told SRF he intends to win a race eventually. It is the best Swiss result in the four years the Gurgl slalom has run.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-11-23-sports-nef-takes-first-world-cup-podium", "first_seen_date": "2026-11-23", "event_date": "2026-11-22", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Tanguy Nef", "Swiss-Ski"]}
